{
  "info": {
    "name": "Ecommerce Backend API",
    "description": "Identity (auth, sessions, roles, permissions) and Catalog (products, categories, brands) HTTP APIs.\n\n**Setup**\n1. `docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up -d`\n2. `npm run migrate`\n3. `npm run seed:identity` then `npm run seed:catalog`\n4. `npm run dev`\n5. Run **Roles > Create Role** (or fetch a seeded role id via psql: `SELECT id FROM roles WHERE name='admin';`) and set the `roleId` collection variable, then run **Auth > Register**.\n\n`accessToken`/`refreshToken`/`roleId`/`permissionId`/`productId`/`productSlug`/`categoryId`/`brandId`/`imageId` are collection variables auto-populated by each folder's create/login requests' Tests scripts — run requests top-to-bottom within a folder the first time.\n\nKnown pre-existing gap: Identity's seeded permission names are dot-separated (`role.create`) while route checks use colon-separated names (`role:create`), so role/permission-protected Identity routes will 403 even for `admin` until that's reconciled. Catalog's own seed (`npm run seed:catalog`) uses colon-separated names consistently with its routes, so Catalog permission checks work as seeded.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
